---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Atur"
  description="How Atur collects, uses, and protects your data."
  canonical="/privacy"
>
  <div class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p><em>Last updated: October 18, 2026</em></p>
      <p>
        Atur ("we", "us") operates the workspace application at
        <a href="https://app.diatur.com"> app.diatur.com</a>. This policy explains what
        data we collect when you use Atur and how we use it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What we collect.</strong> Account information (email and name, including
        what Google or Apple share with us if you sign in with them), the
        workspaces and content you create inside Atur (issues, pages, contacts,
        deals, timesheets), and basic usage data needed to operate the service.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>How we use it.</strong> To provide and improve the service, to send
        transactional emails (account verification, notifications), and to keep the
        service secure.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Where it lives.</strong> Your data is stored securely on managed
        servers around the world. It is encrypted in transit and at rest, and is
        backed up daily.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Website analytics.</strong> This marketing site (diatur.com) uses
        Revklik, a cookieless analytics service, to count page views, traffic sources,
        device types, and clicks on sign-in buttons. It sets no cookies and does not
        record your name or email. The Atur app itself is not tracked.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Sharing.</strong> We do not sell your data. We share data only with
        the infrastructure providers needed to operate the service.
      </p>
      <h2 id="delete-account">Delete your account</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete your Atur account and its personal data at any time, without
        contacting us.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>In the mobile app:</strong> open the <em>Profile</em> tab, tap
          <em>Delete account</em>, type <code>DELETE</code> and confirm.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>On the web:</strong> sign in at
          <a href="https://app.diatur.com">app.diatur.com</a>, open
          <em>Profile &amp; Settings</em>, scroll to <em>Danger zone</em> and choose
          <em>Delete account</em>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>By email:</strong> if you can't sign in, write to
          <a href="mailto:support@diatur.com">support@diatur.com</a> from the address
          on the account and we will delete it for you.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>What is deleted.</strong> Your profile (name, email address, avatar),
        sign-in methods (password, Google and Apple links), active sessions, API keys,
        personal notes, notification settings and workspace memberships. Your
        Sign in with Apple authorization is revoked. Deletion is immediate and cannot
        be undone; the same email address can later be used to create a new account.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What is kept.</strong> Workspaces are shared. A workspace you own passes
        to its earliest-joined admin (or, if there is none, its earliest-joined member);
        a workspace where you were the only member is deleted with your account. Issues,
        comments and time entries you created in a workspace that continues to exist stay
        for the remaining members, shown as "Deleted user" with no link back to you.
        Daily backups taken before the deletion are discarded after 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Contact.</strong> Questions about this policy can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:support@diatur.com"> support@diatur.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
